From: steamac <steamac@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] virtio-snd: macOS CoreAudio backend and runtime audio controls

Make SND=1 build on macOS (PipeWire becomes a Linux-only dependency) with a
CoreAudio backend (audio_backends/coreaudio.rs, written for steamac):

- playback: default-output AudioUnit (follows the system default device) or a HAL
  unit bound to a selected device; the guest format (U8/S16/S32/FLOAT, 8-48 kHz,
  1-2 ch) goes to the unit, which converts. Guest data is copied into a lock-free
  SPSC ring by a pump thread; the real-time render callback only copies out of it.
- pacing: playback messages complete along the device clock (the last callback's
  chunk is interpolated, completions run a host FIFO ahead of the device: one
  device IO buffer + safety offset, plus the configurable buffer, default 40 ms,
  capped at the guest buffer minus two periods), so the guest never runs faster
  than real time and its hw_ptr moves smoothly. latency_bytes reports the FIFO
  plus CoreAudio's downstream latency (IO buffer, safety offset, device + stream
  latency, unit). Device and device-rate changes are picked up once a second.
- the ring is filled whatever the unit state; after START and after an underrun
  the callback plays silence until the ring holds a FIFO's worth (at most a
  FIFO's time), so one late guest write does not become a run of underruns.
- STOP plays out what the guest already saw completed and holds the rest (pause);
  RELEASE waits for that, then completes everything pending. I/O queued outside
  PREPARE..RELEASE is completed at once (VIRTIO_SND_S_BAD_MSG) instead of being
  held, which would make the guest's next prepare fail forever.
- underruns (a gap followed by more data) are counted and logged once a second.
- capture: HAL input unit on the default input device, started only between
  START and STOP (microphone permission is asked then), AudioConverter to the
  guest format/rate, follows default-input changes while recording.
- STEAMAC_SND_DUMP=/path.wav records the playback stream as handed to CoreAudio;
  STEAMAC_SND_TRACE=1 logs PCM commands with the host stream state (ring, clock,
  completions, callbacks) and a once-a-second heartbeat on stderr.

Runtime controls (include/libkrun.h): krun_snd_set_output_device,
krun_snd_set_volume, krun_snd_set_buffer_ms, usable before or after
krun_start_enter (registry like krun_display_resize).

Device hardening: unknown control codes, invalid/mismatched stream ids in I/O
requests and failed PREPARE/START/STOP no longer panic the worker; event-queue
buffers are no longer logged as errors.
